  "remainingOverviewSelectorsSample": [
    "/* v6.64 embedded Overview 2.0 - no router, no blank second page */\n    .overviewTwoShell",
    "/* v6.68 Overview 1.0 dense executive grid\n       Design target: dense/minimal like Overview 2.0, but with compact KPI cards and a clearer executive layout.\n       Scoped to Overview 1.0 only so Overview 2.0 remains untouched. */\n    #overviewOne.tabPage",
    "/* v6.75 Looker Studio-style axis treatment for Overview 1.0 bar charts:\n       - Hide Y-axis tick values on bar charts while keeping the Y-axis title.\n       - Keep only month ticks on the X-axis, no X-axis title.\n       - Give the top-left legend more room above the grid.\n       - Let the plot/grid area feel wider and taller inside the same compact card system. */\n    #overviewOne .areaCustomers .chartBox,\n    #overviewOne .areaUnits .chartBox,\n    #overviewOne .areaRpac .chartBox,\n    #overviewOne .areaAvg .chartBox",
    "/* v6.70 Overview 1.0 mover tables: remove the extra card shell.\n       Tables should look like the Overview 2.0 raw table panels: title/buttons sit on the canvas,\n       and the table itself begins at the dark header with no padded white area-card around it. */\n    #overviewOne .moverArea",
    "/* v6.71 focused cleanup:\n       - Keep mover tables as raw tables (no extra area card), but add a single table outline so they don't feel unfinished.\n       - Give bar-chart legends breathing room above the plotting grid without changing the overall layout. */\n    #overviewOne .moverArea .tableScroll",
    "/* v6.72 focused table restore:\n       v6.70/v6.71 made the mover tables table-only, but the broad td rule also flattened\n       negative/positive colors and allowed the Inactive badge to get clipped. Restore those\n       visual states without bringing back the extra area card background. */\n    #overviewOne .moverArea .tableScroll",
    "/* v6.73 focused table pass:\n       - Slightly widen the mover-table rail.\n       - Keep raw table layout with only the table outline, no extra area-card background.\n       - Preserve inactive badges by making the name column able to show the pill cleanly. */\n    #overviewOne .grid",
    "/* v6.130 upgraded Overview replacement:\n       Overview 2.0 now replaces Overview, but the working 1.0 dropdowns are\n       mounted inside the active Overview so every control shares one state. */\n    #overviewOne.legacyOverviewReference:not(.active)",
    "/* v6.154 top analytics cockpit + fixed analytic panel styling\n       Goal: keep the filled/wide dashboard, but use horizontal space for additional analytics\n       instead of making the revenue line chart and KPI cards overly wide. Also restores the\n       v6.152 insight panels to compact card/table styling so they do not render as oversized text. */\n    #overviewTwo .overviewTwoShellV150",
    "/* v6.152 analytics restored: compact cards, not raw giant text. */\n    #overviewTwo .o2InsightGridV152",
    "/* v6.155 cleaner deep-dive presentation\n       Keep every analytic metric, but stop showing all four lower panels at once.\n       Remove presentation/reset buttons and make the insight controls feel like compact story buttons. */\n    #overviewTwo .o2FeatureDockV153",
    "/* The old four-card insight grid is no longer used, but keep a safety style if older markup appears. */\n    #overviewTwo .o2InsightGridV152",
    "/* v6.156 scalable pace timeline + cleaner hierarchy\n       Keep all metrics, but combine Monthly YoY and YTD Gap Path into one scalable Year Pace card.\n       This prevents the top from becoming a wall of cards as the year grows from 6 to 12 months. */\n    #overviewTwo .overviewTwoShellV150",
    "/* v6.158 read-first cleaner layout\n       Same analytics, less clutter: compact top cards, inline story controls, and a scalable pace ribbon. */\n    #overviewTwo .overviewTwoShellV150",
    "/* v6.160 command-bar layout cleaner\n       Structure fix: use the width for a top metric command bar, then one main story row.\n       No analytics removed. Revenue Trend appears once; Year Pace and Management Readout sit in a right-side stack. */\n    #overviewTwo .overviewTwoShellV150"
  ],
